    {
      "id": "claim_2da4dff8325142e98edc0b219bbb9b17",
      "statement": "A JWKS validation wrapper built from ocm-sdk-go's authentication.NewHandler is applied around the entire chi router in cmd/server/main.go (not just the API subtree) whenever AuthPolicy is not 'disabled', fetching signing keys from cfg.JWKCertURL and optionally cfg.JWKCertFile, exempting only '^/health$' via Public(), and storing the verified JWT in the request context for later extraction.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/server/main.go#L392-L422",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be6b22db053cf421a2c49201097b68eef8dc02ae06aacc10242c6044439719c9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_141e18bfa34f4433afd1f3b28cb7882d",
      "statement": "auth.GetCallerIdentityFromJWT retrieves the verified token placed in context by the JWKS wrapper via authentication.TokenFromContext, extracts username/email/clientId from RHSSO claims with a fallback to preferred_username (RHD), and an empty or missing token/username causes auth.Middleware.AuthenticateAccountJWT to reject the request with 401.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/auth/authn.go#L29-L47",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:82b1d9a32c8d4b0de6a30561f45d6749439b044417d7729d6cc5ef803e86bed0:"
