    {
      "id": "claim_6f58115a57574415afcecc55da15cb07",
      "statement": "Client.Connection() is handed to awsapi.NewCloudCredentialsProvider as a method value (accessor) rather than invoked once and its result captured, so backplane-cli's cloud-credential flow always fetches a freshly-resolved connection/token rather than one captured at server boot; the server does call Connection() once at startup solely to fail fast on a non-concrete connection, discarding the result.",
